# Lighthouse — web runtime credentials.
#
# Copy to `web/.env.local` and fill in. Next.js loads `.env.local` automatically; no
# library and no import are needed. That file is gitignored (`web/.gitignore` has `.env*`,
# which is also why this template has no leading dot — `.env.example` would be ignored
# too, and a template nobody can see is not a template).
#
# Nothing here is required to run the app. `npm run dev` works with this file absent:
# the safety gate, the crisis banner, and the chat all function, and the UI states that
# replies are scripted. That is the "if the API is down, triage still works" property
# from CLAUDE.md, exercised as the default path rather than as an untested branch.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — optional. Turns scripted replies into real ones.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used ONLY to write the assistant's chat replies (`src/lib/intake.ts`). It never sees a
# tier, never proposes one, and its output is never read by the classifier. If you are
# looking at this variable while trying to change how a tier is decided, you are in the
# wrong file — that is the Python side.
#
# NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_. That would ship your key to every student's browser.
#
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL — needed to persist anything at all
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Neon serverless Postgres. The Drizzle schema (`src/lib/db/schema.ts`) is written but has
# never been pushed, so no tables exist yet. Until this is set the chat is stateless: it
# holds a conversation in React state and forgets it on refresh.
#
# Day 6 (counsellor queue) and day 8 (audit log, retention) both hard-depend on this.
#
# Free tier at https://neon.tech — create a project, copy the pooled connection string.
# Format: postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Day 9, not yet used by any code
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The HF Space serving the turn classifier. Live chat calls it with a timeout and degrades
# to gate-only triage on failure (CLASSIFIER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS in src/lib/config.ts).
# Seeded demo data ships with precomputed scores, so the demo never depends on it.
# LIGHTHOUSE_CLASSIFIER_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIGHTHOUSE_PII_KEY — required once anything is stored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AES-256-GCM key for the PII map: the only place a student's real names, places and
# contact details exist, and they are sealed with this before they touch the database.
#
# A database dump without this key yields redacted transcripts and nothing else. That is
# the entire point — so in a real deployment it lives in a secret store, NOT beside
# DATABASE_URL, because holding both is equivalent to holding plaintext.
#
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
#
# Rotating it makes every existing sealed span permanently unreadable. There is no
# recovery path and that is deliberate.
LIGHTHOUSE_PII_KEY=
